    [BugFix][PD] Support single-head NHD GQA caches in MooncakeConnectorV2 (#19824)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    MooncakeConnectorV2 treats the first KV block dimension as the head
    count, so an NHD GQA cache shaped `[tokens, 1, dim]` is interpreted
    incorrectly even when TP leaves exactly one KV head per rank.
    
    Infer the layout from each layer's cache spec and actual tensor shape
    during registration. Publish byte-equivalent `[1, tokens, dim]` transfer
    metadata for contiguous single-head NHD blocks while retaining the
    original tensor, base address, and block stride. Reject multi-head NHD,
    ambiguous multi-head shapes, and noncontiguous NHD block payloads.
    Layout detection does not read environment variables.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. GQA backends using NHD can use MooncakeConnectorV2 when TP leaves
    one local KV head per rank. Existing HND behavior is retained except
    that shapes with equal head/token dimensions and multiple heads are
    explicitly rejected because shape alone cannot distinguish their layout.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    By CI.
    
